M-03 step 9: rollback/negative cases
M-03 case veto-block: 9 vetoes cap max support at 16 < required 17 -> never activates
M-03 case lost-majority-reset: S-c shows the 14-day clock restarts from the re-gained majority day, not the first majority day
M-03 case vote-expiry: a validator silent 24h flips to 'no' (TrustedVotes expiresAfter 24h); S-f shows a 1-day dip on day 5 discards 5 days of accumulated hold, moving activation from day 14 to day 20
M-03 case unsupported-activation: an unsupported amendment that reaches majority has firstUnsupportedExpected = majority time + 2 weeks; if it then activates, servers without code support are blocked (setAmendmentBlocked)
M-03 case single-validator: trusted=1 -> required=1 (exception: >= not >)
M-03 case truncation: post-fix threshold uses integer division floor(t*67/100); effective required fraction at t=25 is 68%, at t=24 is 70.83%, at t=2 is 100%
M-03 case one-way: once enabled an amendment can never be disabled, only superseded by a subsequent amendment
